  "description": "SparrKULee is a repository of speech-evoked auditory EEG responses from normal-hearing native Dutch/Flemish speakers at KU Leuven, who listened to continuous speech stimuli across multiple sessions. This NEMAR re-host contains 80 of the original 85 participants, as five subjects are access-restricted at the source repository. The dataset supports research on neural speech tracking and auditory EEG decoding.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded in BDF format while participants listened to speech stimuli (short stories and varying stories) across 11 session types. Participants were aged 18-30 years with normal hearing (≤30 dB HL). Some recordings lack an adequate number of triggers and cannot be accurately aligned with the stimulus.",
